**Given:**

dfrac{{3sqrt 2 + 2sqrt 5 }}{{sqrt {45} + sqrt {18} }}

**Concept used:**

In such questions we use rationalization by multiplying appropriate quantity to both numerator and denominator.

**Calculation:**

In such questions, solving for the left-handed side (LHS),

LHS; 

= dfrac{{3sqrt 2 + 2sqrt 5 }}{{sqrt {45} + sqrt {18} }}

= dfrac{{3sqrt 2 + 2sqrt 5 }}{{3sqrt {5} + 3sqrt {2} }} times dfrac{3sqrt{5} - 3sqrt{2}}{3sqrt{5}-3sqrt{2}}

= dfrac{{9sqrt {10} - 18 + 30 - 6sqrt{10}}}{{45-18 }}

= dfrac{{3sqrt {10} + 12}}{{27 }}

= dfrac{12}{27} + dfrac{3sqrt{10}}{27}

= dfrac{4}{9} + dfrac{1sqrt{10}}{9} .... (1)

= a + bsqrt{10} .... (2)

Comparing (1) and (2),

a = 4 / 9 and b = 1 / 9.

**The values of a and b are 4/9, 1/9.**
